@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Login as the Provider (Jane)
# @name loginProvider
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Store token and Provider User ID
@providerToken = {{loginProvider.response.body.token}}
@providerUserId = {{loginProvider.response.body._id}}

### 2. Add Morning Availability (Happy Path)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-10-01",
  "startTime": "09:00",
  "endTime": "13:00"
}

### 3. Add Afternoon Availability (Happy Path - Does not overlap)
# @name createAfternoonBlock
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-10-01",
  "startTime": "14:00",
  "endTime": "17:00"
}

### Store ID of the afternoon block to test delete later
@blockId = {{createAfternoonBlock.response.body.data._id}}

### 4. Attempt to add OVERLAPPING Availability (Error Testing)
# Expected Result: 409 Conflict (Because 12:00-15:00 overlaps with both blocks above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-10-01",
  "startTime": "12:00",
  "endTime": "15:00"
}

### 5. Attempt Invalid Time Logic (Error Testing)
# Expected Result: 400 Bad Request (Start time is after end time)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/availability
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-10-02",
  "startTime": "18:00",
  "endTime": "10:00"
}

### 6. Provider views their own schedule
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/availability/me?date=2026-10-01
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}

### 7. Customer views Provider's schedule (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/availability/{{providerUserId}}?date=2026-10-01

### 8. Provider deletes the afternoon block
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/availability/{{blockId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{providerToken}}